Third-party material

OpenMMLab-derived files, and how:

- cfm_model_zoo/configs/: model configuration files derived from MMDetection's
  configs (Copyright OpenMMLab). Some were renamed, merged with their _base_ files
  or edited (for example dataset paths).
- cfm_model_zoo/split_backbones.py: split_forward re-implements, split in two, the
  forward() of MMDetection's and MMSegmentation's ResNet and SwinTransformer backbones.
- cfm_model_zoo/split_models.py: compatibility patches to MMDetection's BERT
  language-model wrapper; the Split classes subclass MMDetection / MMSegmentation models.

RepPointsV2 code (cfm_model_zoo/legacy/):

- cfm_model_zoo/legacy/ is ported from the Mask RepPoints V2 code of Microsoft's
  Swin-Transformer-Object-Detection
  (https://github.com/SwinTransformer/Swin-Transformer-Object-Detection), licensed under
  the Apache License, Version 2.0: see
  third_party_licenses/Swin-Transformer-Object-Detection-LICENSE.txt. That code builds on
  MMDetection v2 and the RepPoints V2 implementation (https://github.com/Scalsol/RepPointsV2),
  and includes code adapted from CornerNet (https://github.com/princeton-vl/CornerNet;
  corner pooling, Gaussian focal loss).
- Its CondConv mask head (condconv.py) is modified from AdelaiDet's CondInst
  (https://github.com/aim-uofa/AdelaiDet), and its ATSSAssignerV2 (assigners.py) is adapted
  from ATSS (https://github.com/sfzhang15/ATSS). AdelaiDet and ATSS are licensed for
  non-commercial purposes only (third_party_licenses/AdelaiDet-LICENSE.txt and
  third_party_licenses/ATSS-LICENSE.txt), which is why this package excludes commercial use.
- RepPoints V2 is licensed under the MIT License, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation:
  see third_party_licenses/RepPoints-LICENSE.txt (the LICENSE file of the repository above).
- CornerNet is licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License, Copyright (c) 2018, University of
  Michigan: see third_party_licenses/CornerNet-LICENSE.txt.

Pretrained weights

No pretrained weights are distributed with this package. They are downloaded from their
publishers and remain under the publishers' terms: OpenMMLab's (through mim, and for the two
DDQ-DETR models from OpenMMLab's download server); for RepPointsV2, the Mask RepPoints
V2 Swin-T 3x release of Microsoft's Swin-Transformer-Object-Detection; and, for GLIP and
GroundingDINO's language model, bert-base-uncased from the Hugging Face Hub (downloaded by
transformers on first use).

See cfm_model_zoo/configs/README.md, "Attribution", for the papers to cite.
